media-sam-van-boxtel-climbers-crag", "web_url": "https://www.portsidepro.com/podcast-feed/ep-131-how-brands-are-wasting-money-on-social-media-sam-van-boxtel-climbers-crag", "guest_name": "Sam Van Boxtel", "guest_title": "Founder at Climbers Crag", "categories": ["digital-marketing"], "short_description": "In this episode, Cole and Sam discuss the most common mistakes outdoor brands make on social media, the value of social in the outdoor space, why social media is important for brand building, what metrics to track, and much, much more!", "podcast_length": "59:57"}, {"id": "aad1c653-5b45-4d81-ac2f-74edd030e126", "episode_id": "75f56310-05dd-4251-93ca-e178ecafde6d", "cms_item_id": "68225dfc7bb476527f8c48a8", "chunk_index": 0, "content": "John Peabody (00:00:01): The future is in social media and short form content and very snackable content and stuff like that. But that's just not true. That's just proven not true at all. People want that. But people also want to go very, very deep on things and love going deep on everything.\n\nCole Heilborn (00:00:22): Welcome to the Backcountry Marketing podcast. I'm your host, Cole Hy one. On this podcast, you'll hear from leaders in the outdoor marketing industry discuss the gritty details of their work, as well as the latest challenges and lessons they're learning along the way. If you want to hone your craft and become a stronger marketer than this podcast is for you. This podcast is produced by Portside Productions, an outdoor film production company based in the Pacific Northwest. Welcome to the Backcountry Marketing Podcast. My name is Cole Holborn. Today I'm sitting down with John PBD. He's the director of branded content at Gear Patrol Studios. John, how are you,\n\nJohn Peabody (00:00:59): Cole? I'm doing really well. Thanks so much for having me, man.\n\nCole Heilborn (00:01:02): Yeah, thank you for joining this conversation today. Where do we find you? How's your day going?\n\nJohn Peabody (00:01:08): Day's going well. I'm here in Brooklyn working from home. It's a nice day and I'm well caffeinated, so I feel ready to go for I guess my first podcast ever.\n\nCole Heilborn (00:01:23): Well, maybe, I mean, we were just talking about this before we started to record, and you've done quite the radio. You've had quite the radio background, and so I think you're probably fairly qualified for a podcast if you've been on the radio.\n\nJohn Peabody (00:01:37): Yeah. Well, thanks. I'll try. It's true. I've done some radio, done some photography, done some video and stuff, and it's all kind of blurring, I guess, now into just general content, but this feels very professional seeing you on this special software here and everything, so I don't know. I'm going to try not to be too intimidated here.\n\nCole Heilborn (00:02:02): So you said you're in Brooklyn. How long have you been based there? Is that where Gear Patrol is located?", "token_estimate": 539, "speakers": ["John Peabody", "Cole Heilborn"], "start_timestamp": "00:00:01", "end_timestamp": "00:02:02", "podcast_index": 133, "episode_name": "EP: 133 How to Beat the Attention Economy | John G Peabody | Gear Patrol", "slug": "ep-133-director-of-branded-content-john-g-peabody-gear-patrol", "web_url": "https://www.portsidepro.com/podcast-feed/ep-133-director-of-branded-content-john-g-peabody-gear-patrol", "guest_name": "John Peabody", "guest_title": null, "categories": ["brand"], "short_description": "Do you struggle to create content that really resonates with your audience? Are you frustrated by shorter attention spans? On this episode, Cole sits down with John Peabody to talk about how to beat the attention economy and create GOOD content that matters.", "podcast_length": "1:09"}]
